{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_leyp2mvagsrctnfp6mzmhomyp6kbeq6iiuqtda65sei7u2abdg7q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Verification complete — all 56 differential tests pass in every configuration; the Rust translation needed no fixes.**\n\n## Result\n\n| Gate | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `cargo check` compile errors | none (clean, 0 warnings) |\n| `SYMBOLS.md` — `nm -D` parity | **7/7** C symbols exported by Rust, 0 missing, 0 non-libc undefined |\n| `CONFIGS.md` — Phase B | **28/28** rows pass across randomized inputs (fixed seed) |\n| stdout byte-for-byte | matches (no driver binary exists; the library's own 8 `printf` lines compared instead) |\n| `ERRORS.md` — Phase C | **25/25** rows have a passing error-path test |\n| Feature combos | 0 features declared → default / `--no-default-features` / `--all-features` × debug + release, all pass |\n\n## What was built\n\n- `translation/SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md` — Phase A artifacts, all boxes checked.\n- `translation/tests/common/mod.rs` — loads **both** `.so`s via `libloading`; no Rust function is called directly. Includes a `fork()`-based `capture_stdout` (cargo's harness can't see the libraries' raw fd-1 `printf` output) and `run_isolated` for crash-parity checks.\n- `tests/phase_b_configs.rs` (27 tests), `phase_b_stdout.rs` (2), `phase_c_errors.rs` (25), `phase_d_symbols.rs` (2).\n- `translation/run_all.sh` — builds C + Rust, diffs `nm -D`, sweeps all feature combos × profiles, plus an alternate-C-codegen sweep.\n\n## Two findings worth your attention (both C-side UB, not translation defects)\n\n1. **`modeselect(mode_selector < 0, …)`** — `mode_selector % 4` is negative in C, so `modes[mode_index]` reads *before* the array. The C is not self-consistent: linked into a small driver it `SIGSEGV`s for `-1/-2/-3`, but called from inside the test process it survives and returns a garbage-derived value. No equality is assertable; the test records both outcomes and requires each to be a clean return or a memory fault. `INT_MIN` is special-cased — `INT_MIN % 4 == 0`, so it's in-bounds and its full result is asserted equal.\n\n2. **`hash_time_value` at gcc `-O3`** — `hash *= 0x1F` overflows `int`, and `-O3` reassociates the loop on that UB: `hash_time_value(0)` returns `0x7E4B2761` instead of the `0xF6F605A` that `-O0`, `-O2` and `-O3 -fwrapv` all produce. The Rust reproduces the wrapping two's-complement value, i.e. it matches the C as `CMakeLists.txt` actually builds it (no `-O` flags). `-O3` without `-fwrapv` is excluded from the sweep for that reason.\n\nOne environment note: crates.io is unreachable through the proxy, so all cargo invocations use `--offline` (`libloading 0.8.9` and `libc` were already in the local registry cache). `libc` was added to `[dev-dependencies]` alongside `libloading` for `fork`/`dup2`/`waitpid`. Nothing in `c_src/` was modified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":628,"cache_read_input_tokens":95899,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":628,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1d7d48c0-db1f-410d-a7dc-2100fe65ef3a","uuid":"6cba83b6-8973-4205-a8ad-f45948339a73","timestamp":"2026-09-05T15:46:50.461Z"}
